                            self.diag_arena.allocator(),
                            "A class cannot implement a primitive type like '{s}'. It can only implement other named object types.",
                            .{raw},
                        );
                        try self.report(impl_node, TsCodes.class_implements_primitive, msg);
                        continue;
                    }
                }
                try self.reportUnresolvedTypeRefHeritage(impl_node, type_params);
                const target_t = self.lowererLowerWithTypeParams(impl_node) catch types.Primitive.unknown;
                // TS2422 — the implements target is not an object type
                // (bare type parameter, primitive, or union). Fires before
                // (and instead of) the TS2420 assignability check, matching
                // upstream's `!isValidBaseType` guard. Mirrors the
                // interface-side TS2312 (`reportInterfaceExtendsNonObject`).
                if (try self.classImplementsNonObjectTarget(impl_node, target_t, type_params)) {
